  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "route templates are unreachable: omega-c-sharp emits reference.attribute with the attribute name only and publishes no string-literal argument, so [Route(\"api/[controller]\")], [HttpGet(\"{id}\")] and app.MapGet(\"/orders\", ...) state the verb and the declaration site but never the path",
      "a class-level [Authorize] cannot be told apart from a method-level one: both lie within the class span and the overlay has no negative join, so authorization is stated for actions only",
      "a C# 12 primary constructor declares its parameters on the class rather than inside a definition.constructor, so aspnet.injection.constructor does not see them",
      "which type argument of AddScoped<TService, TImplementation> is the service and which the implementation is not recoverable: both arrive as reference.type inside the same call span, so both are stated as registered types",
      "types named in a constructor body, and not only in its parameter list, are also stated as injected",
      "extension-method and factory-lambda registrations, source-generated controllers, conventional route tables and runtime container selection remain outside what any Pack states"
    ]
  },
